        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017-sch-1-sec-46-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "hasPower",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The corporation has power in the market.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) A corporation is taken for the purposes of this section to have a substantial degree of power in a market if:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017-sch-1-sec-46-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "hasPowerInMarket",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The power in the market is determined by the temporal intervals.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) that corporation and a body corporate that is, or that corporation and 2 or more bodies corporate each of which is, related to that corporation, together have a substantial degree of power in that market."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017-sch-1-sec-46-ss-3-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "hasPowerInMarketOverTime",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The power in the market over time is determined by the temporal intervals.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) that corporation and a body corporate that is, or that corporation and 2 or more bodies corporate each of which is, related to that corporation, together have a substantial degree of power in that market."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017-sch-1-sec-46-ss-3-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "diffusesPower",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The power diffuses from the corporation to its related bodies corporate.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) a body corporate that is related to that corporation has, or 2 or more bodies corporate each of which is related to that corporation together have, a substantial degree of power in that market;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017-sch-1-sec-46-ss-3-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "hasCogAI",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The corporation has cognitive abilities.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) A corporation is taken for the purposes of this section to have a substantial degree of power in a market if:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017-sch-1-sec-46-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46(4) Misuse of market power",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017#sch-1-sec-46-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "(4) In determining for the purposes of this section the degree of power\nthat a body corporate or bodies corporate have in a market:\n\n(a) regard must be had to the extent to which the conduct of the\nbody corporate or of any of those bodies corporate in that\nmarket is constrained by the conduct of:\n\n(i) competitors, or potential competitors, of the body\ncorporate or of any of those bodies corporate in that\nmarket; or\n\n(ii) persons to whom or from whom the body corporate or\nany of those bodies corporate supplies or acquires goods\nor services in that market; and\n\n(b) regard may be had to the power the body corporate or bodies\ncorporate have in that market that results from:\n\n(i) any contracts, arrangements or understandings that the\nbody corporate or bodies corporate have with another\nparty or other parties; or\n\n(ii) any proposed contracts, arrangements or understandings\nthat the body corporate or bodies corporate may have\nwith another party or other parties.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) In determining for the purposes of this section the degree of power\nthat a body corporate or bodies corporate have in a market:\n\n(a) regard must be had to the extent to which the conduct of the\nbody corporate or of any of those bodies corporate in that\nmarket is constrained by the conduct of:\n\n(i) competitors, or potential competitors, of the body\ncorporate or of any of those bodies corporate in that\nmarket; or\n\n(ii) persons to whom or from whom the body corporate or\nany of those bodies corporate supplies or acquires goods\nor services in that market; and\n\n(b) regard may be had to the power the body corporate or bodies\ncorporate have in that market that results from:\n\n(i) any contracts, arrangements or understandings that the\nbody corporate or bodies corporate have with another\nparty or other parties; or\n\n(ii) any proposed contracts, arrangements or understandings\nthat the body corporate or bodies corporate may have\nwith another party or other parties.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017-sch-1-sec-46"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017-sch-1-sec-46-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017-sch-1-sec-46-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017-sch-1-sec-46-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6b3e1aabf0acae9f1371729c848c6a32525133678dbf8457411bed8260945b3e",
      "skos:note": "Regard must be had to the extent to which conduct is constrained by competitors or suppliers."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017#sch-1-sec-46-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "46(4) Misuse of market power",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 7,
      "values:originalText": "(4) In determining for the purposes of this section the degree of power\nthat a body corporate or bodies corporate have in a market:\n\n(a) regard must be had to the extent to which the conduct of the\nbody corporate or of any of those bodies corporate in that\nmarket is constrained by the conduct of:\n\n(i) competitors, or potential competitors, of the body\ncorporate or of any of those bodies corporate in that\nmarket; or\n\n(ii) persons to whom or from whom the body corporate or\nany of those bodies corporate supplies or acquires goods\nor services in that market; and\n\n(b) regard may be had to the power the body corporate or bodies\ncorporate have in that market that results from:\n\n(i) any contracts, arrangements or understandings that the\nbody corporate or bodies corporate have with another\nparty or other parties; or\n\n(ii) any proposed contracts, arrangements or understandings\nthat the body corporate or bodies corporate may have\nwith another party or other parties."
    },
