    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017-sch-1-sec-46-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46(5) Misuse of market power",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017#sch-1-sec-46-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "(5) For the purposes of this section, a body corporate may have a\nsubstantial degree of power in a market even though:\n\n(a) the body corporate does not substantially control that market;\nor\n\n(b) the body corporate does not have absolute freedom from\nconstraint by the conduct of:\n\n(i) competitors, or potential competitors, of the body\ncorporate in that market; or\n\n(ii) persons to whom or from whom the body corporate\nsupplies or acquires goods or services in that market.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) For the purposes of this section, a body corporate may have a\nsubstantial degree of power in a market even though:\n\n(a) the body corporate does not substantially control that market;\nor\n\n(b) the body corporate does not have absolute freedom from\nconstraint by the conduct of:\n\n(i) competitors, or potential competitors, of the body\ncorporate in that market; or\n\n(ii) persons to whom or from whom the body corporate\nsupplies or acquires goods or services in that market.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017-sch-1-sec-46"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017-sch-1-sec-46-ss-5-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "be99670d6a5dc5e9571323d50d4e4ba38be88cb90fa2ff9c77135930ec5ec868",
      "skos:note": "A body corporate may have a substantial degree of power in a market even though it does not substantially control that market or has absolute freedom from constraint by competitors."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017#sch-1-sec-46-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "46(5) Misuse of market power",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 7,
      "values:originalText": "(5) For the purposes of this section, a body corporate may have a\nsubstantial degree of power in a market even though:\n\n(a) the body corporate does not substantially control that market;\nor\n\n(b) the body corporate does not have absolute freedom from\nconstraint by the conduct of:\n\n(i) competitors, or potential competitors, of the body\ncorporate in that market; or\n\n(ii) persons to whom or from whom the body corporate\nsupplies or acquires goods or services in that market."
    },
