    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017-sch-1-sec-46-2-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46(5) Misuse of market power",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017#sch-1-sec-46-2-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "(5) For the purposes of this section, a person may have a substantial\ndegree of power in a market even though:\n\n(a) the person does not substantially control that market; or\n\n(b) the person does not have absolute freedom from constraint by\nthe conduct of:\n\n(i) competitors, or potential competitors, of the person in\nthat market; or\n\n(ii) persons to whom or from whom the person supplies or\nacquires goods or services in that market.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) For the purposes of this section, a person may have a substantial\ndegree of power in a market even though:\n\n(a) the person does not substantially control that market; or\n\n(b) the person does not have absolute freedom from constraint by\nthe conduct of:\n\n(i) competitors, or potential competitors, of the person in\nthat market; or\n\n(ii) persons to whom or from whom the person supplies or\nacquires goods or services in that market.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017-sch-1-sec-46-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017-sch-1-sec-46-2-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017-sch-1-sec-46-2-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d02e5a5494240822f57372843c0b86951e7e15f538be6935e8260e53adb2c9d6",
      "skos:note": "A person may have a substantial degree of power in a market even though they do not substantially control the market or are not absolutely free from constraint by others."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-misuse-of-market-power-act-2017#sch-1-sec-46-2-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "46(5) Misuse of market power",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "(5) For the purposes of this section, a person may have a substantial\ndegree of power in a market even though:\n\n(a) the person does not substantially control that market; or\n\n(b) the person does not have absolute freedom from constraint by\nthe conduct of:\n\n(i) competitors, or potential competitors, of the person in\nthat market; or\n\n(ii) persons to whom or from whom the person supplies or\nacquires goods or services in that market."
    },
